Enable GUI on SLES
==========================


# 1. Force register the module using lowercase letters
sudo SUSEConnect -p sle-module-desktop-applications/15.5/x86_64

# 2. Refresh your system repository cache
sudo zypper refresh

# 3. Install the graphical desktop pattern
sudo zypper in -t pattern gnome

# 4. Set the system to boot into the desktop interface
sudo systemctl set-default graphical.target

# 5. Launch the desktop login manager screen
sudo systemctl start display-manager


========== If SUSE License expired, install the OpenSUSE packages =============

# 1. Clean out the broken/expired SUSE subscription repositories
sudo zypper removerepo --all

# 2. Add the free openSUSE Leap 15.5 Main and Update repositories
sudo zypper addrepo -f http://download.opensuse.org/distribution/leap/15.5/repo/oss/ free-base-oss
sudo zypper addrepo -f http://opensuse.org free-update-oss

(if need to reinstall them, remove them first):
	|_ sudo zypper removerepo repo-oss repo-update opensuse-oss opensuse-updates

# 3. Clean all old metadata and pull from the new free paths
sudo zypper clean -a
sudo zypper --no-gpg-checks refresh

# 4. Install the GNOME Desktop using openSUSE's pattern name
sudo zypper in -t pattern gnome

# 5. Route the system boot sequence to launch the GUI
sudo systemctl set-default graphical.target
sudo systemctl start display-manager
